      ],
      "text": "**I’d skip strenuous outdoor exercise in Jurong right now.** NEA’s latest haze update says air-quality stations in Singapore were at **Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy** levels, with a forecast of **PSI 150–230 for October 17**. ([haze.gov.sg](https://www.haze.gov.sg/))\n\nFor a decision about *this hour*, check the **West-region 1-hour PM2.5** reading in NEA’s myENV app or haze.gov.sg: NEA advises reducing strenuous activity if it’s **56–150 µg/m³**, and avoiding strenuous activity if it’s **151 µg/m³ or higher**. ([haze.gov.sg](https://www.haze.gov.sg/?trk=public_profile__reactions-text&utm_source=openai)) It’s also hot—about **29°C now**, with a forecast high of **33°C**—so an indoor workout is the safer choice. ",
